# L §6.1 What same does: "A thing's entries are such facts: an entry only one side states stands, and on a day on
# which the two sides' entries into one kind disagree, whatever depends on the thing being alive there is a HOLE-SAME
# hole (in a binding over that kind, an unknown member, §5.11)"; L §8.1 HOLE-SAME "<p> and <q> are one, but <x>
# differs on <d>: <a> (<row>) and <b> (<row>)". a enters ola from 2026-01-01, b from 2026-03-01: on 2026-02-01 the
# joint model's own count over persons meets ola as an unknown member (a hole naming both); on 2026-04-01 both sides
# agree (1). A member is closed: a's def, read as a.cnt, binds over a's entries only (1 on 2026-02-01).
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "a.tally" sha256 "d87340c7b1f0312deb3488dfae254a77c6aed15d26a7aa84939c231254b2ea13"
  use b = "b.tally" sha256 "827058fa5c25a40d4131ab455794ecdc24d518a7436a6cb775c73afdbaff646e"
  same a.persons = b.persons
  same a.ola = b.ola

source s "ustalenia"

input d1: date
input d2: date

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  d1 = 2026-02-01
  d2 = 2026-04-01

ask feb: count(p in a.persons on d1)
ask apr: count(p in a.persons on d2)
ask own: a.cnt
=== a.tally
model a
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

kind persons

input day: date

def cnt: int = count(p in persons on day)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  persons + [ola] lives 2026-01-01..
  day = 2026-02-01

ask q: cnt
=== b.tally
model b
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

kind persons

input day: date

def cnt: int = count(p in persons on day)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  persons + [ola] lives 2026-03-01..
  day = 2026-02-01

ask q: cnt
=== expect
apr: 1
  cut 2026-10-20
feb: ?"a.ola and b.ola are one, but the entry into a.persons differs on 2026-02-01: 2026-01-01.. (a.v) and 2026-03-01.. (b.v)" (a.ola, b.ola)
  cut 2026-10-20
own: 1
  cut 2026-10-20
